  "measurementLimits": [
    "Root explicitly released CPU window after lifecycle timing. Root reserved itself to coding/light reads, but this is a shared Mac with background desktop/browser processes; no OS cache flush, CPU affinity or guaranteed host isolation. Feasibility only, not a final performance acceptance result.",
    "Only three independent processes per variant. First list means first list in a new process, with a newly copied DB and warm OS file cache; no cold-disk claim.",
    "Read timings include JSON parsing and, for compressed rows, SQL owner checks, gzip, exact byte count and SHA-256. Decoder never resolves Observation references.",
    "Write timings include owner SELECT, JSON.stringify, optional parse/gzip/hash/envelope and upsert in one transaction per batch; fixture creation and explicit GC are outside timing.",
    "The 292 changed-identity and 1434 unchanged-history batches are separate transactions here; do not add them and claim actual end-to-end capture latency.",
    "Updated rows append the exact retained occurrence reference; synthetic new IDs use one retained occurrence and a copied control. These payloads benchmark shape/codec, not new identity evidence or legal replay permission.",
    "The prototype follows state-style admission: serialize/parse/validate owner before the size threshold. Extra parsing contributes to the 32 KiB write overhead; this is not a lower bound for optimized future designs.",
    "Explicit GC between batches makes this a controlled allocation workload, not an end-to-end SDK measurement. Common SDK mutation feeds/hooks are not included.",
    "measuredPeakRssBytes is native process high-water RSS captured after workload plus exact verification, before the final DB file SHA read; it includes fixture/maps. Read-phase sampled RSS is reported separately.",
    "WAL size is a final file-size snapshot, not total bytes written or write amplification. Final VACUUM timing includes two checked TRUNCATE checkpoints.",
    "Trial JSON startedAt is sampled during final serialization. The authoritative process interval is execution.json startedAt/finishedAt per trial."
  ]
